item.aggregated_output:
1://! Coordinator session handoff.
2://!
3://! When the coordinator session restarts — Claude Code update, app
4://! restart, crash, or the supervisor's restart ceiling — the incoming
5://! session starts with none of what the operator told the outgoing one.
6://! This module is the engine half of the fix:
7://!
8://! * **Storage.** The outgoing session writes a short handoff through
9://!   `boss handoff write` (`FrontendRequest::SetCoordinatorHandoff`).
10://!   The engine keeps it as one JSON value in the `metadata` table of its
11://!   own database — coordinator-private state, never in a repo — stamped
12://!   with the write time and the spawn token of the coordinator session
13://!   that was live when it was written. The engine never synthesizes a
14://!   handoff from logs or transcripts; the coordinator writes it.
15://!
16://! * **Delivery.** Every *fresh* coordinator session (`start_new` in
17://!   [`crate::coordinator_tmux`]) is launched with a session-start brief
18://!   as its initial prompt — the same mechanism worker sessions use for
19://!   their initial prompt — so the incoming session consumes the handoff
20://!   on its very first turn without anyone typing anything. An adopted
21://!   session (engine restart, coordinator survived) keeps its own context
22://!   and gets no brief; that path is the existing prompt-change nudge.
23://!
24://! * **Three distinct states, none silent.** [`HandoffState`] separates
25://!   "a handoff is present", "no session ever wrote one", and "one is
26://!   stored but cannot be read". The brief spells out which applies, and
27://!   for a present handoff, whether the session that just ended wrote it
28://!   or whether it is a leftover from an earlier session (an abrupt kill
29://!   before the outgoing session refreshed it). A missing or stale
30://!   handoff is reported as such, never passed off as "nothing to hand
31://!   off".
32://!
33://! Abrupt termination is handled on the writer side by policy, not by a
34://! shutdown hook: the coordinator prompt (`bossSystemPrompt` in
35://! `BossPaneModel.swift`) tells the session to refresh the handoff at
36://! natural boundaries — whenever the operator states a fact that changed
37://! the world, a decision, or a prohibition — so a handoff always exists
38://! as of the last such boundary, and the brief's writer/age stamps make
39://! any gap visible. See `tools/boss/docs/coordinator-session-handoff.md`.
