854:/// Parse `claude --version` stdout, e.g. `"2.1.237 (Claude Code)\n"` — the
855:/// first whitespace-separated token, when it is a dotted run of digits.
856:/// Mirrors the soft-parse shape `conformance::version_pin::parse_codex_version`
857:/// uses for `codex` (which instead takes the *last* token; the two CLIs put
858:/// the version in different positions).
859:fn parse_claude_version(stdout: &str) -> Option<String> {
860:    let line = stdout.lines().next()?.trim();
861:    let version = line.split_whitespace().next()?;
862:    let looks_like_semver = !version.is_empty()
863:        && version
864:            .split('.')
865:            .all(|part| !part.is_empty() && part.chars().all(|c| c.is_ascii_digit()));
866:    looks_like_semver.then(|| version.to_owned())
867:}
868:
869:/// Bound on how long the version probe may block a tokio worker thread
870:/// before giving up. Both call sites (`start_new`, the attach path) are
871:/// async, so an un-timed `claude` invocation — a hung wrapper script, a
872:/// stalled filesystem, a node startup that never returns — would otherwise
873:/// park a worker indefinitely.
874:const CLAUDE_VERSION_PROBE_TIMEOUT: Duration = Duration::from_secs(2);
875:
876:/// Probe the `claude` binary on `PATH` for its version. Best-effort and
877:/// silent on any failure (binary absent, non-zero exit, unparseable output,
878:/// or timeout) — a coordinator session must never fail to launch because
879:/// this probe did, and a failed probe must read as "can't tell", never "no
880:/// update". Uses `tokio::process::Command` (not `std::process::Command`)
881:/// because both call sites run on the async attach/creation path.
882:async fn probe_installed_claude_version() -> Option<String> {
883:    let output = tokio::time::timeout(
884:        CLAUDE_VERSION_PROBE_TIMEOUT,
885:        tokio::process::Command::new("claude").arg("--version").output(),
886:    )
887:    .await
888:    .ok()?
889:    .ok()?;
890:    if !output.status.success() {
891:        return None;
892:    }
893:    parse_claude_version(&String::from_utf8_lossy(&output.stdout))
894:}
